   "source": [
    "Understanding Exceptions\n",
    "\n",
    "Exception handling in Python allows you to handle errors gracefully and take corrective actions without\n",
    "stopping the execution of the program. This lesson will cover the basics of exceptions, including how to use try,\n",
    "except, else, and finally blocks.\n",
    "\n",
    "What Are Exceptions?\n",
    "\n",
    "Exceptions are events that disrupt the normal flow of a program. They occur when an error is encountered\n",
    "during program execution. Common exceptions include:\n",
    "\n",
    ". ZeroDivisionError: Dividing by zero.\n",
    "\n",
    ". FileNotFoundError: File not found.\n",
    "\n",
    "· ValueError: Invalid value.\n",
    "\n",
    "· TypeError: Invalid type."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1c7683da",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "name 'b' is not defined\n",
      "division by zero\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# 1. NameError \n",
    "try :\n",
    "    a = b \n",
    "    c = 1/0\n",
    "except NameError as ex :\n",
    "    print(ex)\n",
    "except ZeroDivisionError as ex :\n",
    "    print(ex)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. ZeroDivisionError  \n",
    "try :\n",
    "    c = 1/0\n",
    "except ZeroDivisionError as ex :\n",
    "    print(ex)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. ValueError \n",
    "try : \n",
    "    a = int(input(\"enter\"))\n",
    "except ValueError as ex :\n",
    "    print(ex)\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "eaea91db",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "0.2\n",
      "end of code \n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# try except else finally\n",
    "\n",
    "try :\n",
    "    c = 1/5\n",
    "except ZeroDivisionError as ex :\n",
    "    print(ex)\n",
    "\n",
    "else :             #it excecute when there is no error \n",
    "    print(c)\n",
    "finally:\n",
    "    print(\"end of code \")  #it execute alltimes whenever error is there or not "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "747f74cc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "name 'b' is not defined\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# exception \n",
    "try :\n",
    "    1/0\n",
    "\n",
    "except Exception as ex :  # if we write exception so it works for all types of error \n",
    "    print(ex)\n"
   ]
  }
